; Customer parts. Every part is a full 48x72 canvas with identical anchoring: head centred on the x=24 line
; (cols 0..23 | 24..47), feet on row 71, counter line on row 52: the shop draws the canvas at stage y 96 so row 52
; meets the counter top (y 148) and rows 0..51 show above it (hat tips from row 0, head rows 13..36, shoulders from
; row 38, hands resting on the counter at rows 48..51). Rows 52..71 (belt, legs, boots) are behind the counter.
; Layer order: body, head, hair, face, accessory. _0/_1 are the idle-bob frames: bodies keep hands and feet and
; drop the shoulders (rows 0..46) 1px; heads, hair and faces drop 1px; the goat chews; the lantern flickers.
; Faces (face_happy, face_neutral, face_annoyed) are the mood expressions, drawn over any head and hair: brows rows
; 21..22, eyes rows 24..26 at cols 16..19 | 28..31, cheeks rows 27..28, mouth rows 29..32 at cols 20..27. Heads
; carry only nose and ears; hair never covers the face zone (the beard leaves room for the mouth).
; Palette swap (shaders/palette_swap.gdshader) may remap ONLY these indices, per part:
;   cloth A (bodies, witch hat): e f g        cloth B (trim, belts, hat bands, trousers): i j k
;   hair (hair parts): 1 2 3                   skin (hands on bodies): r s -> the head's (main, shade) pair
; Head skin pairs (main, shade): head_round r,s; head_long s,t; head_square t,2.
; Everything else (outline 0, iron 7 8 9, apron 6 9, straw 4 5 6, faces, boots, goat, lantern) is fixed.

